  "analysis": "We need to implement a solution for Codeforces 1519C - Berland Regional. The problem requires computing, for every k from 1 to n, the total strength of the region when each university sends their top groups of k students (in blocks of size k). For a university with m students, only full blocks count, so the contribution for a given k is the sum of the top floor(m/k) * k skills, i.e., the prefix sum up to index floor(m/k) * k after sorting that university's skills in descending order. Across all universities, we sum these contributions for each k. A correct and efficient solution groups students by their university, sorts each group, builds prefix sums, and for k from 1 to size_of_group, adds pref[floor(m/k) * k]. The overall complexity is roughly O(n log n) due to sorting plus linear passes over all groups, which fits the constraints since the total n across test cases is ≤ 2e5.",
